{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE PHONE APP BAR — REFERENCE §7.2, AppBar.dc.html
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Two variants and no third. HIG allows a navigation bar back + title + ONE
  action, and the rule is what keeps the bar readable at a glance:

    root   a tab destination. 52px row of [88px · centred small title · 88px],
           then a large Playfair title that collapses on scroll. This is the
           page's only <h1>.
    child  a pushed screen. 44px back · title + optional sub, both truncating ·
           at most one action.

  ── THE GRID WIDTHS ARE NOT DECORATION ───────────────────────────────────────

  Root is `88px minmax(0,1fr) 88px` — two equal 88px rails so the centred title is
  centred against the BAR rather than against whatever happens to be in the slots.
  Child is `44px minmax(0,1fr) auto`, left-aligned, because a child title sits
  beside its back button and has no symmetry to keep.

  ── AND THE AVATAR IS A SHEET, NOT A LINK ────────────────────────────────────

  It opens Quick settings. There are deliberately NO separate Aa or language
  buttons in the phone bar (REFERENCE §18.5): they live in that sheet, because a
  bar with back, title, search, Aa, language and avatar is the nav-clutter
  anti-pattern the standards reject.

  Args
    variant   'root' | 'child'                     default 'root'
    title     the page title                       required
    sub       child only; must ADD information, never repeat the title
    back      child only; the href for the back button
    search    show the search icon                 default: root
    share     show the share action                default: child
    avatar    show the avatar → Quick settings     default: root
    initials  the avatar's letters
#}
{% set _variant = variant|default('root') %}
{% set _root    = _variant == 'root' %}
{% set _search  = search is defined ? search : _root %}
{% set _share   = share  is defined ? share  : not _root %}
{% set _avatar  = avatar is defined ? avatar : _root %}

<div class="ag-appbar ag-appbar--{{ _root ? 'root' : 'child' }}">
  <div class="ag-appbar__row">

    {% if _root %}
      {% if _search %}
        <a class="ag-appbar__icon" href="/discover" aria-label="Search Africa GATES">
          <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
               stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
            <path d="m20 20-3.6-3.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </a>
      {% else %}<span></span>{% endif %}
    {% else %}
      <a class="ag-appbar__icon" href="{{ back|default('/') }}" aria-label="Back">
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path>
        </svg>
      </a>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="ag-appbar__title">
      {% if _root %}
        {# Hidden at rest and faded in on scroll — the large title below is the one
           being read until then. `aria-hidden` stays off: it is the same string, and
           a screen reader hearing it twice is better than a sighted-only title. #}
        <span class="ag-appbar__small">{{ title }}</span>
      {% else %}
        <b>{{ title }}</b>
        {% if sub is defined and sub %}<span>{{ sub }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="ag-appbar__end">
      {% if _share %}
        <button type="button" class="ag-appbar__icon" data-ag-share aria-label="Share">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
               stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 3v12"></path><path d="m7 8 5-5 5 5"></path>
            <path d="M5 14v5a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-5"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>
      {% endif %}
      {% if _avatar %}
        <button type="button" class="ag-appbar__icon" data-ag-quick
                aria-label="Account, language and display" aria-haspopup="dialog"
                aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="ag-appbar__av">{{ initials|default('AG') }}</span>
        </button>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if _root %}
    {# The page's only <h1>. It collapses on scroll and the small title above takes
       over; the heading stays in the accessibility tree either way. #}
    <div class="ag-appbar__large"><h1>{{ title }}</h1></div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
